# Chapter 10-11: "The Reason the Dragon Gem Shines"

"You don't think Sakura and Tiga are awful? If I'd known this would happen, I would have... I would have...!"

"Would you have never considered using your miracle to save someone because you cared about your own skin~?"

"Even if I would have done it knowing the consequences, my state of mind would be completely different between knowing and not knowing!"

Apparently aware of her own emotional tendencies, FIloure made this accurate self-analysis while tearfully glaring at Sakura, who sat across from her. 

Sakura, who claimed to be like an older sister to her, frowned troubledly at Filoure's words.

"Even if you say that to me, we're just as troubled, you know~ Subaru-chan and Beatrice-chan understand, don't they~?"

"I don't know why you're bringing me and Beako into this, but I kinda get that this situation was bound to happen somehow."

"Regardless of who's responsible, seeing your exchange makes it easy to guess that Filoure was the one who created the opportunity."

Saying this, Subaru and Beatrice shook their heads in perfect unison, expressing their opinions in response to Sakura's question as they sat nearby.

Incidentally, the seating arrangement in the reception room's sofas now had Emilia, Otto, and Filoure clinging to Emilia's arm on the host side, while Sakura, Subaru, and Beatrice sat side by side on the guest side after moving seats. 

Adding to the reception room's liveliness, Petra who had been there from the start was joined by Rem, who had guided Filoure there.

"Though honestly, Filoure explains pretty much all of this increased volume. More importantly, why are we sitting over here? This combination is weird."

"How dreadful! Emilia, did you hear that? Subaru is trying to separate me, your dearest friend, from Emilia. Could he be an agent of the church...?"

"Any agent of the church would clearly be you."

Beatrice sighed at Filoure's apparently terrified expression. Emilia, whose arm Filoure was clinging to, smiled wryly and patted her friend's head.

"Come now, don't look at Subaru like that, Filoure. Subaru is very, very kind, and he'd never intrude between us. Besides, the relationship between Subaru and me and the relationship between Filoure and me are completely different, aren't they?"

"R-right, I suppose so. ...Incidentally, do you have any preference about which is more important?"

"Huh? Well..."

"Never mind! Don't answer! The scriptures say this too: 'The trials given by the dragon are because of love. Just as gold increases in purity when burned by fire, the soul too, through hardships borne of love, emits a radiance befitting the Dragon's heart'!"

Filoure, burying her face and clinging to the scriptures, was less a devout follower of the Divine Dragon Church and more someone simply covering up inconvenient things with scripture's teachings.

Since she had cut off Emilia's words, hearing about Subaru's current standing in Emilia's affections was also interrupted, leaving Subaru feeling unsatisfied too.

That aside—

"About what we were discussing earlier... Filoure participating in the Royal Selection—does that mean she's taking Priscilla's place?"

Ignoring Filoure who was arbitrarily turning red and pale, Emilia directed her question to Sakura across from her.

At this question, Sakura slightly narrowed her droopy eyes that looked sleepy.

"...At the very least, there's no doubt that Priscilla-chan's death is one of the reasons~ If not, it would contradict the Dragon History Stone's inscription~"

"So the Divine Dragon Church's policy is that they cannot act against the Dragon History Stone, which clearly records five Dragon Maidens as Royal Selection candidates."

"Of course, please don't think we took this opportunity to boldly march into the castle just because that premise collapsed~ Even if Priscilla-chan's absence created a vacancy among the Dragon Maidens, the Church's policy was to maintain distance~"

"But that didn't happen. And the reason for that is..."

Otto deliberately didn't state the conclusion, but everyone's gaze gathered on Filoure—the one who had created the initial ripple that led to this situation.

Feeling uncomfortable under their stares, her throat tightened, and then she clung to Emilia.

"Th-that's not it, Emilia! I never had the slightest intention of becoming your enemy! It was just a coincidence of unfortunate circumstances! A-a-and anyway!"

Pale-faced, Filoure's eyes flew open as she glared at Sakura.

"Anyway, I protest that there's room to question the Church's secrecy-obsessed nature! All of this happened because they raised me sheltered until today! Not that I didn't think it was nice being exempt from the studies other children had to do, but for that to tear me apart from Emilia... I'm not bad, but!"

"There, there, don't cry, Filoure. I'm not angry at all, and I've never thought of the other Royal Selection candidates as enemies."

"E-Emiliaaah...!"

Filoure's agitated heart was soothed by Emilia's gentle hand stroking her head.

Watching this exchange, Sakura gasped and covered her mouth with her hand.

"My, normally this is where things drag on forever, but Emilia-chan is really good at handling Filoure-chan... Is there a trick to it~?"

"Leaving aside jokes about how all Filoures are neutralized by Emilia-tan's fluffy包容力... What exactly did Filoure come here for?"

From her behavior so far, it was clear this wasn't a declaration of war regarding the Royal Selection. Surely she hadn't rushed through the royal capital just to whine and make excuses?

"Would that surprise you?"

"It wouldn't surprise me at all, actually."

"I agree, but that won't move the conversation forward..."

"Wait a minute. Do you really think I'm that thoughtless? I admit I often act without thinking things through, but today is different. I actually have a plan."

"A plan?"

"Yes, a plan! I don't want to participate in the Royal Selection. But I want to fulfill my duties as a Saint by using my miracle. So I want Emilia, my friend, to hide me while I secretly save the people of Pristera! How's that!"

"Is this a villain organization's criminal scheme from a morning kids' show?"

It was a plan so full of holes even a child could see through it. Since the goal was helping people, it wasn't even a criminal scheme, but the biggest problem was that Sakura had already found her out.

In other words, her scheme had stumbled at the starting line.

"Also, it'd probably be bad if we got accused of kidnapping the Divine Dragon Church's Saint."

"Emilia-nee-sama has that tendency too—people who don't realize they're walking bombs are dangerous, you know."

"Eh, does that mean Emilia and I are perfect for each other...?"

"Is that really the part where you blush?"

For whatever reason she felt confident, Filoure's plan was swiftly rejected.

Subaru thought Filoure was underestimating the situation a bit too much. She'd been trying to steer the conversation toward withdrawing from the Royal Selection—but—

"You can't just throw away the qualifications of a Royal Selection candidate, can you?"

"Emilia-tan..."

"I've been studying hard every day too. I think I understand the kingdom much better than at the beginning... and about the强制力 of what's written in the Dragon History Stone too. I had my own reasons for wanting to participate in the Royal Selection, but even if I didn't, I don't think I could have refused."

Looking at Filoure clinging to her arm, Emilia spoke seriously.

It made sense that Royal Selection candidates couldn't refuse. Last night, she'd discussed it with Garfiel and Petra—the covenant with the Dragon in the Dragon Kingdom is strong and deep-rooted.

In fact, Felt once tried to refuse participation in the Royal Selection. But she was forced to participate in exchange for Rom's safety when they tried to take her away.

This represented a kind of强制力—that the kingdom would stop at nothing to make the Dragon Maidens recorded in the Dragon History Stone participate in the Royal Selection.

Emilia was saying the same thing applied to Filoure.

"But... but this isn't something I wished for?"

"Yes, I'm sure it isn't. I think if you couldn't make the insignia shine, this wouldn't have happened. ...But the Dragon Gem shone, and you were chosen. You should understand the meaning of that better than anyone, Filoure."

"Uu..."

At Emilia's almost maternal words, Filoure weakly hung her head.

Filoure was a nun of the Divine Dragon Church. Needless to say, as someone who held faith and reverence for the Dragon, she would be in the best position to understand the强制力 of the Dragon History Stone's inscription.

Her behavior so far could even be called childish escapism.

But—

"Then... yes, how about this? Filoure and I form a friendship alliance. That way, I'll cooperate with anything to help Emilia become king. Then, for the Royal Selection..."

"Thank you, Filoure. —But I really, really don't want that."

Quietly, but with unshakeable firmness, Emilia clearly asserted this.

At the nobility in her silver-bell voice, Filoure's throat let out a small "Eep." So Filoure could see, Emilia reached into her bosom and opened her palm holding the insignia.

Instantly, the Dragon Gem's overflowing red radiance brightly illuminated the reception room of the Margrave's residence.

"As I said before, I had my own reasons for wanting to participate in the Royal Selection from the very beginning."

Showing the brightness of the Dragon Gem, Emilia spoke as if to let Filoure hear.

Emilia's initial motivation for participating in the Royal Selection was to borrow the power of the Dragon's Blood kept in the royal castle to save her frozen homeland. But as time passed, meeting people and learning things, Emilia's feelings about the Royal Selection were also changing.

Still, that initial wish probably wouldn't fade or disappear.

And—

"The others too. Crusch-san has her reasons, Anastasia-san has hers, Felt-chan has hers... Priscilla had hers. Everyone participated in the Royal Selection with their own goals. No, that's not right."

"Not right? What's not right?"

"Surely, people who can make the Dragon Gem shine have reasons to want to participate in the Royal Selection... things they can only achieve by doing so. If that's true, then you must have them too."

"I... have them too...?"

At Filoure, blinking dazedly, Emilia smiled bravely and cutely.

She had suggested supporting her friend Emilia's wish now that she'd become a candidate, but considering that Filoure's wish didn't quite convince her.

With just that reason, she couldn't认可 her as one of the participants in this Royal Selection of the Kingdom of Lugnica.

"Please, don't immediately say no because of your overwhelmed feelings when you first heard about this. Think about it very, very carefully. They probably won't let you refuse participation in the Royal Selection. But I really don't want someone who's only participating because they have no choice to sit in Priscilla's chair."

—These were strong words, an expression of will, and also a prayer.

"—"

At Emilia, who had passionately expressed her feelings head-on, Filoure blinked. In the tension rising between the two at zero distance, no one spoke.

In the ensuing silence, Subaru and everyone else refrained from inserting themselves. —So that no unnecessary impurities would mix with the choice that followed.

"—Here."

The one who rippled the surface of that silence was Emilia, watching Filoure from closest. She narrowed her long-lashed eyes and offered the insignia in her hand to Filoure.

Filoure reflexively accepted it. —Even if it was unconscious, the Dragon Gem of the insignia didn't choose when to shine.

"—If I were to participate in the Royal Selection..."

The Dragon Gem shone in Filoure's hand just as it had in Emilia's as she murmured this. Blinking with light the same color as her own eyes, Filoure declared:

What faith would she profess in the face of the inescapable fate of the Royal Selection thrust upon her?

"I want to reform the relationship between the country and the church until now. So that people in the castle won't hesitate to reach out to the church, and people in the church won't hesitate to reach out to the castle, for silly reasons."

"—"

"If I were to become king, I'd create a country where no one hesitates to help others."

It was nothing more than an imposed ideal, still lacking in细节.

But it was Filoure's own wish, born from growing up as a member of the Divine Dragon Church, living, and feeling the constraints and frustrations she wanted to break through and improve.

And no one would laugh at Filoure for professing this, calling her just a numbers-filler reluctantly participating in the Royal Selection, forcibly carried on a palanquin by those around her.

"...We really should have turned away this unannounced visit."

Otto muttered this quietly at Filoure's conclusion.

Without his hat and cloak, he ran his fingers through his grayish hair habitually, evaluating what had happened here.

Actually, Subaru could understand Otto's feelings in wanting to say that.

"At this late stage, an ultra-strong rival appears."

"I think this is a ridiculous act of aiding the enemy... The troublesome part is that it was our leader who prompted it."

"Don't worry. When Emilia-tan's opponents are stronger, somehow, she just gets better."

"If you want to encourage me, could you at least say something better!?"

"Even I sympathize with Otto this time. But..."

Breaking off there, Beatrice narrowed her eyes and gazed dazzlingly ahead—at Emilia and Filoure, and Subaru agreed.

Certainly, if you only looked at what happened, you might call it foolish. He could even picture the amusing image of Roswall collapsing to his knees when he heard the report later.

But it was worth it. In exchange for the appearance of an ultra-strong rival, without a doubt—

"—I definitely won't lose to Filoure either."

—Emilia, aiming to be king, had undoubtedly grown from this experience.







