# Chapter 10-11: "The Reason the Dragon Gem Shines" (Continued)

"—And so, I humbly accept the request to participate in the Royal Selection."

Placing one hand on her chest and making the insignia shine brightly with the other, Filoure declared this proudly, fearlessly, as if nothing in the world could stop her.

The location was the royal castle—not the throne room where they were always summoned whenever something happened, but a conference room apparently used for somewhat more compact discussions. In a space about the size of a school classroom, a round table was placed where roughly twenty people could face each other. Apparently, meetings of the Wise Men's Council and the castle's civil officials were often held in this conference room.

"You know, on the day the Royal Selection started, after Subaru was chased out of the room, we all moved and had our discussion here in this conference room."

"Ah, behind the scenes while I was getting completely trashed by Julius."

"I still can't remember that... but Subaru, you fought with Julius? You made up afterwards... right? That's why you two are very, very close now."

"Whether me and that guy are very, very close aside, it was definitely a necessary event for me and Emilia-tan to become very, very close."

At Emilia's hushed explanation, Subaru twisted his lips in response.

In this world where Julius's name still hadn't returned, he didn't want to delve too deeply into how those involved remembered Subaru's pathetic state that day, even as a lesson.

Fortunately, today's conference room had many empty seats, so almost none of those involved from that day were present. —After all, this was what you'd call a secret meeting, with each camp sending minimal representatives; even from Emilia's camp, only Emilia, Subaru, and his partner Beatrice had been admitted.

Though, one of these extremely limited participants—the old man with distinctive long whiskers who had welcomed them—happened to be one of those involved from that day.

That old man—Microtoff McMahon of the Wise Men's Council—looked at Filoure, who had undergone a refreshingly pleasant change of heart.

"Hmm. As one who issued the request, this answer is extremely welcome... but may I ask again? Though permission was granted, how did it come about that Emilia-sama and Natsuki-dono are accompanying you here?"

"This morning before coming to the castle like this, I consulted with them. Emilia is my irreplaceable friend, and Subaru is her knight... Really, I would have liked to bring everyone from Emilia's camp who supported my declaration of resolve, but..."

"If you'd done that, both I and the church would lose face, you see~"

When Filoure responded to Microtoff's question, Sakura, accompanying her as the church's sole representative, said this with a troubled expression.

Filoure looked dissatisfied with this answer, but having Emilia's camp members trailing along in droves at her formal appearance would be strange, so Sakura's opinion was probably more appropriate.

However, Subaru's impression and Microtoff's as he stroked his long whiskers seemed to differ in what they found striking about Filoure's words.

The wise elder narrowed his intelligent eyes, interjecting his characteristic "Hmm" sigh—

"Friends, you say? Filoure-dono of the Divine Dragon Church and Emilia-sama."

"...Is that what this is about? Still on about how Emilia-tan is a silver-haired half-elf while Filoure is a nun of the Divine Dragon Church?"

"Subaru, really..."

Emilia chided Subaru, who had unintentionally leaned forward at the muttered words.

But here, aside from Subaru and Beatrice, they had no reliable camp companions. So Subaru had to speak up on everyone's behalf and give Microtoff a piece of his mind.

As the primary knight entrusted with Emilia, he had to fight against unreasonableness.

"Microtoff-san, you should know about Emilia's efforts over this past year and a half. Knowing all of that, I want the important people of this country to stop looking at her through biased lenses. Half-elf, or whatever—can't we just move past that?"

"Saying 'move past that' rather ignores popular sentiment, I'm afraid. It's perfectly clear that aside from appearance and race, there's no connection between that Witch and Emilia-sama... but that alone carries great weight. Surely you understand this."

"Guh..."

Microtoff made Subaru, who had attacked quite aggressively, back down with his experienced rhetoric. Once again, the problem was the common sense rooted in the inhabitants of this world—something Subaru couldn't truly feel.

And this didn't apply only to Emilia, a silver-haired half-elf.

"Inevitably, your becoming a Royal Selection candidate as a nun of the Divine Dragon Church will be met with great surprise by the people. This also greatly bends established practice. It was an extremely troubling decision."

"...Yes, I think I understand that. But—"

"Hmm. But, what might that be?"

"—. But if so, why did you go this far to include me in the Royal Selection?"

The question Filoure voiced was only natural.

Microtoff's wording hinted that the castle side wasn't exactly welcoming a Royal Selection candidate from the Divine Dragon Church with open arms.

"I'm a nun of the Divine Dragon Church... I understand it's natural to strictly adhere to the Dragon History Stone's inscription, but even with Priscilla Barielle's death, the fact remains that we began the Royal Selection with five candidates possessing the qualifications of maidens. The inscription hasn't been bent."

"Or has the Dragon History Stone's inscription been updated? Did it rewrite itself to say that when a maiden is lost, we should find a substitute and move them up?"

"No, no report has come in that the Dragon History Stone's inscription has changed. However, regarding this, rather than our intentions, we should probably call it a matter of popular sentiment."

"Popular?"
"Sentiment?"

Subaru and Emilia tilted their heads, questioning Microtoff's answer. Then Microtoff lowered his voice slightly.

"This will become known eventually, but let's keep it confidential, at least within this room. It seems rumors are circulating among the common people. —That the Saint of the Divine Dragon Church saved Duke Karsten."

"—!"

"The castle enforced a gag order regarding this matter. Of course, information seeps out like raindrops even when sealed tight... but it's even spread specifically that this Saint shares the same characteristics as the lost Lugnica princess."

"That means practically all the information has leaked!"

Microtoff's face clouded as if this were a regrettable matter, but if true, the castle's information control had failed miserably.

"I hate to think it, but Filoure... you weren't so happy about saving Crusch-san that you went around gleefully boasting about your achievement, were you?"

"You agree?"

"Don't agree! Besides, I did no such thing! I have discretion, you know! Well, I might have told people close to me, wanting to use it as material to persuade the church people. But would I go around spreading it in the city?"

"Hmm, Beako?"

"I'd call it gray, very close to black."

Subaru largely agreed with Beatrice's harsh assessment.

Sorry to Filoure, who was stamping her feet in frustration, but no matter how much she insisted she hadn't done it, her impression so far was that the aura of "she probably did something like that" wouldn't quite disappear.

In any case, regardless of who caused the rumor to spread—

"Then maybe Filoure making the insignia shine is also rumored? And everyone's upset that it would be strange not to include Filoure as a Royal Selection candidate?"

"It hasn't gone that far yet. However, the announcement of Priscilla-sama's death will soon be made public. If Filoure-dono's existence is known by then, naturally voices demanding her participation in the Royal Selection will flood the streets."

"So before that happens, they're laying the groundwork in advance..."

If Filoure's participation was already a foregone conclusion anyway, moving things forward quickly would make things clearer for everyone. While he understood such adult maneuvering, it still bothered him a bit that Filoure truly had no right of refusal.

If she hadn't discussed things with Emilia beforehand, Filoure would have ended up participating in the Royal Selection with the worst possible mindset, lacking the necessary spirit for a candidate.

"Come now, don't make such a sour face, Subaru-chan. Things worked out well enough in the end, so isn't the process fine~?"

"...Sakura-san, are you okay with this? Originally, Filoure wasn't supposed to be let out of the church, right? Participating in the Royal Selection was unplanned, wasn't it?"

"—Regardless of whether one desires it or not, a leaf has no choice but to be tossed about by the wind and water."

"—"

At Sakura, who had suddenly lowered her voice, Subaru was momentarily speechless.

In that one word was a poignant emptiness—a hollow resignation like that of a withered old tree with a great cavity inside.

It almost felt like she wasn't speaking about Filoure at all, but rather expressing her own—Sakura's personal—resignation.

"Well, things will work out as they will~ Besides, even if she herself gets motivated, she's a year and a half behind the others, so it might not even be a contest."

"Sakura! Why do you always have to dampen my enthusiasm! If I'm doing this, I'm going to win... My tenacity is truly Dragon-like!"

"I'm curious, but how is Filoure's casual style of invoking the Dragon like that viewed by the Divine Dragon Church?"

"Probably as blasphemy, I'd say~"

"Blasphemy!!"

It was harsher than expected, and he understood it was apparently not a recommended attitude. Filoure truly maintained a stance far removed from the typical image of a saint.

At any rate, with answers to most of his questions, Subaru had roughly grasped the purpose of this secret meeting and why participation was so extremely limited. In other words, this was like an unofficial notice before the official announcement, confirming the intentions and policies of those involved.

Just as he'd thought that far, Subaru suddenly had another concern.

It was—

"Hey, if Filoure becomes a Royal Selection candidate too, does that mean you'll also appoint your own knight, like me and Emilia-tan and the other candidates?"

"Ah, Subaru, you might be mistaken about that."

"Mistaken?"

"Well, it just happens that all the Royal Selection candidates have knights, but that's not absolutely required. After all, Anastasia-san and I didn't have knight contracts with Subaru and Julius from the beginning, right?"

"That's true for me, but Julius was Anastasia-san's knight from the start."

"Ah, is that so? I must remember that properly, for Julius's sake."

While Emilia slightly corrected for the effects of the name removal, Subaru understood her explanation. Certainly, initially Emilia had Roswaal accompanying her as her backer, but Subaru as a knight was absent—or rather, he hadn't earned that trust.

So perhaps knights weren't absolutely necessary for Royal Selection candidates.

"But if you're going to do it, having one adds prestige, I think. What will you do? Who might satisfy the conditions to be by Filoure's side... maybe My Friend?"

"My fure... you mean Tiga? That might be good. Filoure seems very, very close with Tiga too..."

"Ehh? My knight would be Tiga? That doesn't feel special at all."

At Subaru's suggestion, Emilia clasped her hands in front of her chest in enthusiastic agreement, but Filoure herself booed with unbelievable force.

"Well, Tiga is capable, so if appointed knight he'd probably handle it without a hitch, but he's always nagging me, and whenever something happens he immediately suspects me—he lacks the respect and loyalty required of a knight. Besides, even now when he's not a knight, he still follows me around everywhere anyway, so there's no point in specially appointing him as knight. Rejected! I reject it!"

"Well, he'd be your knight, so you can decide as you like... Huh? Actually, normally how are knights appointed?"

In Subaru's case, for example, he had been knighted by Emilia's hand and gained his current position as her knight, but what about Reinhard and Julius?

Acquiring knights shouldn't be limited to Royal Selection candidates, but Subaru felt ashamed of his ignorance about how such contracts worked, even now.

"Hmm, yes. In many cases, it's common for knights to seek a master and swear loyalty for their appointment. However, when it comes to famous knights, it's also common to promise high salaries and good treatment, requesting that they deign to serve you."

"Oh, I didn't expect Microtoff-san to explain. ...Incidentally, do you also employ your own knight, Microtoff-san?"

"My house also has many who have served long-term and earned our trust. Generally speaking, those who have excellent knights pledging their swords do command a certain respect."

"That is... well, I can understand that."

In fact, the status of having the Sword Saint or the Finest Knight as their primary knight must have added considerable prestige to Felt and Anastasia's names.

The visibility of one's primary knight was also an important barometer in the Royal Selection. —Was Subaru truly able to be a knight who contributed to Emilia's cause? And Crusch, who had dismissed Ferris as her primary knight, would probably consider taking on a new knight in the future.

"—"

He didn't want her to. That wishful, clinging thought, if Ferris had his say, would be Subaru's arrogance in wanting everything to go his own way.

The unavoidable rift that had formed between the two—perhaps with time and calm reflection, a different answer might be found. So until then, he wanted that position to remain vacant.

Yes, with full awareness of his arrogance, Subaru was indulging in sentimentality.

"...Just now, Microtoff-sama said this, didn't he? That for excellent knights, one should ask loudly and insistently for them to come to one's side."

"—? What Betty heard seems quite different in intensity."

"...I also feel the nuance was different."

Clenching her fist tightly, Filoure muttered, suppressing her emotions. Prompted by Beatrice's reaction, Subaru also returned from sentimentality to reality.

Was she the type to hear only what suited her? Filoure had interpreted Microtoff's statement in her own way, and her cheeks were slightly flushed. Her feelings seemed to be running so high that her cheeks were heating up—

"Could it be that Filoure has someone in mind she wants as her knight?"

"—! How did you know... because we're best friends?"

"Yes, perhaps. So, what kind of person are they?"

"I'll say it first, Reinhard is already taken."

"Obviously, Subaru is permanently sold out to Betty and Emilia."

Drawing the attention of Subaru and the other three, plus Sakura and Microtoff in the same room, Filoure smiled meaningfully, "Fufufu," and responding to everyone's gazes, vigorously opened her thick scripture before her.

"Listen, please. In the scriptures, it says this: 'The arm that swings the sword is human; the will that handles life is the Dragon's. The footsteps of the chosen knight turn even bloody ruts into silver paths'!"

"Um, what does that mean?"

"In other words, the one worthy of being my knight is someone recognized by the Dragon!"

The interpretation felt somewhat arbitrary, but ultimately, when it came to knights recognized by the Dragon, Subaru couldn't think of anyone besides Reinhard.

Through various creative interpretations, Emilia, who had cleared the first floor trials of the Pleiades Watchtower, could also be said to meet that condition.

"A Royal Selection candidate becoming another Royal Selection candidate's knight would be an interesting twist, but Emilia-tan already has me, so that development is out."

"Emilia becoming my knight... w-well, that idea does appeal to me. But my expectations and hopes are different. Please don't confuse me anymore."

Subaru said nothing to Filoure, unsure whether to think she was easily swayed or that it couldn't be helped since the comparison was with Emilia.

Ignoring Subaru's consideration, Filoure cleared her throat softly.

"Alright? May I continue? As I said, if I, the Saint of the Divine Dragon Church, stand as a Royal Selection candidate, my knight must be recognized by the Dragon. And as far as I know, there is only one person who fulfills that condition—"

When that title was put forward, only one person inevitably came to mind.

Ironically, it was someone with whom Filoure wasn't just competing for the throne, but someone destined to compete over who was the true surviving member of the Lugnica royal family.

Only Reinhard van Astrea, the Sword Saint and primary knight serving Felt—no—

"—Heinkel Astrea-sama."

— —.
— — — —.
— — — — — —.

"!?"

Feeling as if he'd heard the wrong answer, Subaru's throat let out an ugly sound. But Filoure, having made her declaration, had a smug look on her face, while Emilia and Beatrice beside him, like Subaru, showed surprise, their eyes wide.

Astrea, yes, but a different Astrea than expected—an Astrea discrepancy.

"...Ah, Filoure?"

"Wh-what is it? Everyone's reactions are rather strange, somehow?"

"They would be strange. Please, just once more, let me hear it? Who is worthy of being the knight of the Divine Dragon Church's Saint?"

"So I said, I don't want to keep repeating myself... Heinkel Astrea-sama."

No matter how many times he heard it, the name didn't change, and Filoure tilted her head in confusion.

To her, Subaru and the others' reactions seemed far more incomprehensible. And that made sense. After all, in her mind, the person Heinkel Astrea was—

"—Having overcome the Dragon's Blood that soaked his body and become an immortal knight, one of the Sword Saint lineage—I wish to appoint Heinkel Astrea-sama as my knight."

Yes, Filoure, who had become the sixth Royal Selection candidate, was insisting that the most suitable primary knight for herself, the sixth candidate, was Heinkel Astrea, the Sword Bearer.
